d 'QRPDMCMC': module to provide Multi-Chain Adaptive Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) Estimation and Diagnostics for Quantile Regression for Panel Data with Non-Additive Fixed Effects 
d
d  qrpdmcmc extends the adaptive Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC)
d optimization method in qregpd, the command that implements
d Quantile Regression for Panel Data with Non-Additive Fixed
d Effects (Powell, 2022, Empirical Economics). qrpdmcmc complements
d qregpd by providing an integrated environment for multi-chain
d MCMC estimation and convergence assessment. Users can specify
d multiple chains with independent seeds, combine retained draws
d across chains, and assess convergence, sampling efficiency, and
d draw behavior. The command provides graphical and numerical
d diagnostics, including summary statistics, density, trace, and
d running-average plots, autocorrelation functions, Effective
d Sample Size (ESS), Monte Carlo Standard Errors (MCSE),
d Gelman–Rubin R-hat statistics, Geweke diagnostics, and
d parameter cross-correlations. MCMC draws can be retained from the
d sampling process, saved to disk, and subsequently reloaded,
d allowing diagnostics to be performed without re-estimation and
d supporting reproducible workflows. 
d
d KW: quantile regression
d KW: panel data
d KW: adaptive fixed effects
d
d Requires: Stata version 15,1 and moremama, amcmc from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260928
d
d Author: Kamilla Kosheeva,  Friedrich-Alexander-University Erlangen-Nuremberg (FAU)
